lar-open-pattern: <<~\s*hui\s*>>
lar-close-pattern: <<~\/hui\s*>>
lar-example: <<~ hui>>
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

<!-- hui — an AWAIT-ALL JOIN over the flows its block opens. Fan out, then fan in: the containing
     flow resumes only once every child settles, and a failure in any child reaches the container:

         <<~ hui>>
           <<~ lele "lar:///target-a">>
           <<~ lele "lar:///target-b">>
         <<~/hui>>

     A //hui// gathers and holds the gathering — no member leaves while another still travels. An
     enclosing scope that exits first cancels what remains. `sync` mirrors this head in English and
     delegates here.

     THE PAGE STAYS CLEAR. Coordination governs execution and never layout, so the definition hands
     the compile layer a data annotation naming the discipline and renders nothing. -->

\procedure ~hui()
<span class="lar-hui" data-join="await-all" hidden="true"/>
\end
